  "summary": "The Taiping Rebellion, led by Hong Xiuquan, lasted from 1850 to 1864. EBSCO says the rebels seized Wuchang in 1853 and then captured Nanjing, making it their capital, until Manchu troops took it in 1864. Estimates of the dead differ: about 20 million per EBSCO, and between 20 million and 70 million per History.com.",
